<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Etosha Pan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Etosha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Etosha Pan is a large salt pan in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>, about 120 km long, which fills with water only briefly after heavy rains. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovambo-people">Ovambo peoples</a> collected salt there and traded it widely. It lies at the heart of Etosha National Park, proclaimed as a game reserve in 1907, which is one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>'s best-known wildlife reserves.</p></div>
